  "description": {
    "text": "The CoroCoro Challenge was Battle Festa 2015's second tournament, played in the XY format at every venue: Hiroshima on 3 November, Yokohama on 7 and 8 November, Osaka on 15 November and Nagoya on 29 November 2015. The top three of the October pre-battles at Pokémon Card Gym shops got an Advantage Pass that skipped the First Stage. A win in the Second Stage earned a mirror holo Double Dragon Energy stamped with the event's logo, and the top three of each league won Victory Ring in gold, silver or bronze; the elementary school league's top finishers were also invited to the second Pokémon Ryūō-sen, held that December.",
